  "aiContextParagraph": "The resignation of Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka follows a period of intense parliamentary activity regarding a potential impeachment inquiry. Prior to the announcement, 120 members of the Indonesian House of Representatives had signed a petition initiating a formal process to express their opinion on the vice president's tenure. This legislative push had reached the stage of being scheduled for a plenary session. However, following the confirmation of the resignation by government officials and reports that the vice president submitted his official request to the head of state and the People's Consultative Assembly, the parliamentary proceedings have been officially discontinued. Lawmakers from various factions, including the National Awakening Party (PKB), have confirmed that the impeachment process will not proceed. The government now enters a transition period, with the People's Consultative Assembly mandated to appoint a successor within 60 days.",
